== DownloadEngine 2.0.0

Downloads PubChem assays and compounds for a query and stores them through
the MODIP DataBaseServer.

Since 2.0.0 PubChem is reached through PUG REST
(https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug). PUG SOAP is no longer used.
Assay search still uses NCBI E-utilities through the entrez gem.

Public API, notifications, file layout and the enum constants
(AssayOutcomeFilterType, FormatType, ...) are the same as in 1.x.

Main files:
  lib/download_engine.rb                     DownloadEngine (unchanged API)
  lib/pubchem/service_rest.rb                ServiceRest (replaces ServiceSoap)
  lib/pubchem/rest_client.rb                 HTTP client: proxy, retries, throttling
  lib/pubchem/Assay/assay_table_normalizer.rb  REST CSV -> SOAP-compatible CSV
  lib/pubchem/types.rb                       Enums and value types (no soap4r)

Environment:
  DOWNLOAD_ENGINE_SSL_VERIFY=false  skip TLS certificate checks (only for
                                    servers with an outdated CA bundle)

Build and install:
  gem build download_engine.gemspec
  gem install --local download_engine-2.0.0.gem

Tests (offline):
  ruby -Ilib -Itest -e 'Dir["test/**/*_test.rb"].each { |f| require "./" + f }'

Live check against PubChem (needs network, honors MODIP_PROXY):
  ruby -Ilib test/live_check.rb
